# h713-airplay.service - the AirPlay receiver (profile desktop; docs/tools/h713-airplay.md, userspace/h713-airplay/README.md).
#
# Always on, on purpose: an iPhone, iPad or Mac lists the projector under Screen Mirroring as soon as it is on the same Wi-Fi - the
# box's own access point or the network it joined - and that needs somebody to answer at any time. The receiver does all of the
# protocol and nothing of the picture: mDNS (`_airplay._tcp`, `_raop._tcp`, a responder of its own, so no avahi-daemon in the image),
# RTSP on TCP 7000, the pairing, the encrypted mirror stream (TCP 7100) and screen audio (UDP 6000/6001), the clock towards the
# sender (UDP 7011) and the control socket /run/h713-airplay/ctl (`h713-airplay ctl status`). It decrypts and decodes nothing.
# Idle it costs nothing: every thread blocks in a syscall - no decoder, no GPU, no Wayland connection, no timer.
# * Why two units: the receiver must always be there, the picture only while a phone mirrors. When a sender sets up its stream the
#   receiver connects to /run/h713-airplay-show.sock (h713-airplay-show.socket, pulled in by Wants= below) and systemd starts
#   h713-airplay-show.service, the presenter: a mode unit like h713-kodi.service, so the launcher, the remote, `h713-mode hdmi`, a
#   standby and Conflicts= treat AirPlay exactly as they treat Kodi. The presenter's connection closing ends the session here.
# * Not root: the system user h713-airplay (usr/lib/sysusers.d/h713-airplay.conf), which may connect to the presenter's socket
#   (SocketGroup=); its ports are all above 1024 (mDNS 5353), so it needs no capability. The key pair and the device id live in the
#   StateDirectory /var/lib/h713-airplay, kept across reboots, so that a sender sees the same receiver. The hardening is h713-warp's.
# * After the network and h713-wifi: the access point or the station link is up, and the first announcement goes out on it; an
#   interface that comes later is announced on when it appears.
# * /etc/h713/airplay.conf (the name, the port, the display offered, H.265, audio, takeover, the interfaces) is read at the start:
#   `systemctl restart h713-airplay` after a change.
[Unit]
Description=AirPlay receiver (screen mirroring)
Documentation=file:/usr/local/share/doc/h713-airplay/README.md
After=network.target h713-wifi.service
Wants=h713-airplay-show.socket

[Service]
Type=simple
User=h713-airplay
Group=h713-airplay
ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/h713-airplay run
Restart=on-failure
RestartSec=2s
RuntimeDirectory=h713-airplay
RuntimeDirectoryMode=0755
StateDirectory=h713-airplay
NoNewPrivileges=yes
ProtectSystem=strict
ProtectHome=yes
PrivateTmp=yes
RestrictSUIDSGID=yes
MemoryDenyWriteExecute=yes

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
